%I A399940 #11 Oct 05 2026 13:46:31
%S A399940 0,0,0,0,4,14,58,316,3262,43076,349712,3192928,39711200,444465770
%N A399940 Number of permutations of 1..n such that the Hankel matrix of some subsequence of an odd number of consecutive terms is singular.
%C A399940 a(n) is even for all n, because a permutation and its reversal are either both counted or both not counted.
%F A399940 a(n) = n!-A399939(n).
%e A399940 For n = 5, the only possible subsequences with a singular Hankel matrix are 124 and 12345, and their reversals. There are 12 permutations of 1..5 containing 124 or 421 as a subsequence of consecutive terms. Including also the 2 permutations 12345 and 54321, a(5) = 14.
%Y A399940 Cf. A000142, A399939.
%K A399940 nonn,more,new
%O A399940 0,5
%A A399940 _Pontus von Brömssen_, Sep 30 2026
%E A399940 a(12)-a(13) from _Sean A. Irvine_, Oct 05 2026
